          <h2>👋 Hey — I'm Mr. Phil.</h2>
          <p>
            I teach Technology at DaVinci Academy — code, game design, video, and media arts.
            <strong>You matter. You belong here.</strong> This room is safe to ask questions, get stuff wrong, and try again.
          </p>
          <p class="amp-mini">
            You already bring ideas, languages, jokes, and stories that make class better. I live with Jilly,
            our dogs Bubblegum &amp; Rowan, and our cat Lemon.
          </p>
        </section>

        {% include "about-mr-phil/gallery.njk" %}

        <section class="amp-panel">
          <h2>⚡ How my class works</h2>
          <ul class="amp-bullets">
            <li><strong>You build — I guide.</strong> Learning is something you do, not something I do to you.</li>
            <li><strong>Mistakes = clues.</strong> We fix and try again. That's real learning.</li>
            <li><strong>D20 = mic.</strong> Whoever holds the talking dice speaks. Everyone else listens.</li>
            <li><strong>Free Choice time</strong> — freedom <em>and</em> choice when the main work is done.</li>
            <li><strong>Peers teach too.</strong> Sometimes a classmate explains it better than I can.</li>
            <li><strong>Words matter.</strong> I try to include your world — not just a generic default.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="amp-panel amp-panel--story">
          <h2>💡 Story time: what's a smiley face?</h2>
          <p>
            We were learning about binary. The video said <em>"abstraction is the foundation of all computing."</em>
            I realized a lot of us didn't know that word yet — so I drew a smiley face on the board.
          </p>
          <p class="amp-mini">
            You said: smiley face. Happy. Person. A circle with two dots and a curve. <strong>All correct.</strong>
            Abstraction means keeping the main idea and dropping what doesn't matter. A stick figure is an abstract person.
            At their core, computers are just 1s and 0s — on or off.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="amp-panel">
          <h2>🧠 Don't be a Gort</h2>
          <p>
            A <strong>Gort</strong> believes "that's just how it is" and never asks why.
            I'd rather you think for yourself — question things and form your own conclusions.
          </p>
        </section>

